course: dictionary
lesson: 1032
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives three meanings for boomer, so you need the words around it to know which one the writer means.
explain: The song calls him «a Boomer», and says his back legs worked «like pistons» and covered «Twenty-five feet to a bound». Those clues show a big male kangaroo, so here boomer means a kangaroo.
explain: Now read «OK boomer», a teasing put-down that brushes off an older person's opinion as old-fashioned. Here the clues are the words «OK» and the opinion being ignored. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you are probably right.
fact: A baby boomer is a person born in the years just after the Second World War, roughly 1946 to 1964.
fact: «OK boomer» is slang, a teasing way to brush off an older person's opinion as old-fashioned.
fact: In Australia, a boomer is a large male kangaroo.
fact: Slang can sound rude or cheeky, so think about who you are talking to before you use it.
exercise: «The boomer hopped across the red dirt, huge and strong.» What is a boomer in this sentence? | *A big male kangaroo in Australia | A loud drum | A woolly hat | A baby boomer, born after the Second World War
exercise: Mia's brother says «OK boomer» when Grandad talks about the old days. What does he mean? | A polite way to say thank you | A long story about the past | *A teasing way to brush off Grandad's opinion as old-fashioned | A kind hug
exercise: «My grandad was born in 1955, so he is a boomer.» Which meaning fits? | *A person born in the years after the Second World War | A cheeky put-down | A large male kangaroo | A type of hat
test: What does boomer mean in the song, where it says «a Boomer» with back legs like pistons? | A woolly hat | A baby born in 1950 | *A large male kangaroo | A teasing put-down
test: Roughly which years were the baby boomers born in? | 2000 to 2010 | 1914 to 1918 | 1066 to 1100 | *1946 to 1964
exam: Jayden says «OK boomer» to his nan. What is the best explanation of what he means? | He thinks she is a kangaroo | He is telling her she was born in 1990 | He is thanking her for a hug | *He is brushing off her opinion as old-fashioned, in a cheeky way that can be rude
